        <section id="calculus">
            <h2>Calculus: The Fundamental Theorem</h2>
            <p>Calculus is the mathematical study of continuous change. The fundamental theorem of calculus links the concept of differentiating a function with the concept of integrating a function:</p>
            
            <!-- Escaped LaTeX Fix -->
            <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em;" set:html={"$$\\int_{a}^{b} f(x) dx = F(b) - F(a)$$"} />
        </section>

        <hr>

        <section id="linear-algebra">
            <h2>Linear Algebra: Eigenvalues</h2>
            <p>In linear algebra, an eigenvector is a non-zero vector that changes at most by a scalar factor when a linear transformation is applied to it. The corresponding eigenvalue is the factor by which it is scaled:</p>
            
            <!-- Escaped LaTeX Fix -->
            <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em;" set:html={"$$A \\mathbf{v} = \\lambda \\mathbf{v}$$"} />
        </section>
    </div>

